rates on stacked matrix of dimension `codeword_height × width`\n\n2. **Bit Reversal** (lines 263-272): Single `bit_rev()` kernel over entire stacked matrix\n   ```rust\n   unsafe {\n       bit_rev(\n           &codewords,\n           &codewords,\n           log_codeword_height as u32,\n           codeword_height as u32,\n           width as u32,\n       )\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **Batch NTT** (lines 275-282): Single `batch_ntt()` call over entire stacked matrix\n   ```rust\n   batch_ntt(\n       &codewords,\n       log_codeword_height as u32,\n       0u32,\n       width as u32,  // all columns batched together\n       false,\n       false,\n   );\n   ```\n\n### 4. Row Hashing (BATCHED)\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs`  \n**Lines:** 113-138 (`new_generic_with_hash` method)\n\nRow hashing is applied **to the entire RS-encoded matrix as a single batch**:\n\n```rust\nunsafe {\n    MH::compress_rows(\n        &mut query_digest_layer,\n        matrix.buffer(),           // entire stacked RS matrix\n        matrix.width(),            // total stacked width (all AIRs)\n        query_stride,              // height / 2^k_whir\n        k,                         // log_rows_per_query\n    )\n    .map_err(MerkleTreeError::CompressingRowHashes)?;\n}\n```\n\n**CUDA Kernel FFI:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs` lines 52-68:\n- Calls `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes()` kernel\n- Signature: `(out: *mut Digest, matrix: *const F, width: usize, query_stride: usize, log_rows_per_query: usize)`\n- This kernel hashes `2^log_rows_per_query` strided row hashes together for each query point (231ms, 583 instances in profiling)\n\n### 5. Merkle Tree Construction\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs`  \n**Lines:** 113-172\n\nMerkle tree is built **from the bottom up with layer-wise compression**:\n\n1. **Leaf Layer (Row Hashes)** (lines 130-138): All rows compressed via