el | File/Function | Time | Instances | Purpose |\n|--------|---------------|------|-----------|---------|\n| `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` | merkle_tree.rs | 231ms | 583 | Hash all rows, compute leaf layer (called once, many GPU threads) |\n| `calculate_zero_hash` | (CUDA kernel) | 109ms | 584 | Calculate zero hashes for Merkle tree |\n| `merkle_tree_compress` | merkle_tree.rs | 75ms | - | Compress adjacent pairs for upper layers |\n| `merkle_tree_init` | merkle_tree.rs | 71ms | - | Initialize/compress first layer after row hashes |\n| `batch_expand_pad_wide_kernel` | matrix.rs | 11.7ms | 11997 | Expand/pad columns during stacking (per-AIR columns) |\n| `_CT_NTT` / `batch_ntt_kernel` | ntt.rs | (multiple stages) | - | FFT stages for RS encoding |\n| `bit_rev_permutation` | ntt.rs | - | - | Bit-reversal permutation before NTT |\n\n### Call Chain Summary\n\n```\nCoordinator::prove() [prover/mod.rs:104]\n  └─> GpuDevice::commit() [gpu_backend.rs:61]\n       └─> stacked_commit() [stacked_pcs.rs:48] [MAIN ENTRY]\n            ├─> get_stacked_layout() [stacked_pcs.rs:100]\n            ├─> stack_traces() [stacked_pcs.rs:117]\n            │    └─> stack_traces_into_expanded() [stacked_pcs.rs:134]\n            │         ├─ for each AIR trace: D2D memcpy or batch_expand_pad_wide()\n            │         └─> PleMatrix::from_evals() [poly.rs:53] (invNTT if l_skip > 0)\n            │\n            └─> rs_code_matrix() [stacked_pcs.rs:189]\n                 ├─ batch_expand_pad() [matrix.rs:219] (OR reuse stacked if cached)\n                 ├─ batch_ntt_small() [batch_ntt_small.rs:44] (invNTT stages if l_skip > 0)\n                 ├─ mle_interpolate_stages() [poly.rs:99+] (subset-zeta transform)\n                 ├─ bit_rev() [ntt.rs:67] (bit-reversal permutation)\n                 └─ batch_ntt() [ntt.rs:87] (forward NTT - RS encoding)\n                      └─ ct_mixed_radix_narrow() [ntt.rs:141] (NTT stages)\n                 └─> MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash() [merkle_tree.rs:105]\n                      ├─ compress_rows() [cuda/merkle_tree.rs:52]\n                      │   └─ _poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes() [KERNEL]\n                      ├─ Loop: compress_layer() [cuda/merkle_tree.rs:132]\n                      │   └─ _poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer() [KERNEL]\n                      └─ Root D2H copy [merkle_tree.rs:163]\n```\n\n### Key Insights\n\n1. **Traces are batched together**: All common_main traces from all AIRs are stacked into one matrix and processed together, not sequentially per-AIR.\n\n2. **Column-wise stacking is sequential**: The loop at lines 145-179 in `stack_traces_into_expanded()` processes each per-AIR column separately, which could be a bottleneck if there are many small AIRs.\n\n3. **NTT is applied once to the entire stacked matrix**: Not per-AIR, so it benefits from batching.\n\n4. **Row hashing is a single kernel**: Processes all rows of the stacked matrix with 2^k_whir rows hashed together per query point.\n\n5. **Merkle tree build is bottom-to-top sequential**: Each layer depends on the previous, but within each layer, all pairs are processed in parallel.\n\n6. **No synchronization between per-AIR commitments**: Cached/preprocessed traces are committed separately after the main batch commit, allowing some parallelism in that phase."}],"totalDurationMs":81905,"totalTokens":73033,"totalToolUseCount":40,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":68678,"output_tokens":3128,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1222},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":3128,"cache_read_input_tokens":68678,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1222,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":23,"searchCount":5,"bashCount"