{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KUu2ujHtW1WrQKfrTekMAe","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h-35-/// Fp as a subfield, which means operations by the two are compatible, which is important.  The\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h-36-/// irreducible polynomial was chosen to be the simplest possible one, x^4 - B, where 11 is the\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h-37-/// smallest B which makes the polynomial irreducible.\ncrates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h:38:struct FpExt {\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h-39-    /// The elements of FpExt, elems[0] + elems[1]*X + elems[2]*X^2 + elems[3]*x^4\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h-40-    union {\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h-41-        Fp elems[4];\n--\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fp.h-49-///\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fp.h-50-/// The Fp class wraps all the standard arithmetic operations to make the finite field elements look\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fp.h-51-/// basically like ordinary numbers (which they mostly are).\ncrates/cuda-common/include/fp.h:52:class Fp : public bb31_t {\ncrates/cuda-common/include/fp.h-53-  public:\n/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fp.h-54-    /// The value of P, the modulus of Fp.\ncrates/cuda-common/include/fp.h-55-    static constexpr uint32_t P = 15 * (uint32_t(1) << 27) + 1; / bb31_t::MOD"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011cVGJYxsFhcbEPdAFJ8jJc","session_id":"7b26f810-a2da-49ad-94ae-b745d8ecf3f5","uuid":"fd93aabc-8a8c-432b-ad88-c0eb0724dd39","timestamp":"2026-04-12T23:59:21.440Z"}
