{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D7icT1FE1Y7Je9gZFGZiye","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1500-batch-stacking-scatter-kernel\n2\t\n3\tThe `stack_traces_into_expanded()` function in `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` iterates over every trace column (~106K at APC 300) issuing individual CUDA API calls (cudaMemcpyAsync or batch_expand_pad_wide kernel launch) per column. At ~1us CPU overhead per call, this loop costs ~100ms—about 25% of the 404ms Trace Commit phase and 6% of STARK excl trace. Replacing the per-column loop with a single batched scatter kernel that processes all column copies in one GPU launch eliminates this CPU-side overhead, reducing Trace Commit by ~100ms at APC 300 with negligible impact at APC 0 (only ~4K columns).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XVrvupcMHZGasj5E377JPx","session_id":"7b26f810-a2da-49ad-94ae-b745d8ecf3f5","uuid":"a843115c-15e2-40b8-b278-0d1c5baf58ab","timestamp":"2026-04-13T00:02:29.089Z"}
