{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvdncVabE6AMNdSguTG17e","type":"tool_result","content":"apc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n---\nplan.md\n---\n# 2026-04-13-1500-batch-stacking-scatter-kernel\n\nThe `stack_traces_into_expanded()` function in `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` iterates over every trace column (~106K at APC 300) issuing individual CUDA API calls (cudaMemcpyAsync or batch_expand_pad_wide kernel launch) per column. At ~1us CPU overhead per call, this loop costs ~100ms—about 25% of the 404ms Trace Commit phase and 6% of STARK excl trace. Replacing the per-column loop with a single batched scatter kernel that processes all column copies in one GPU launch eliminates this CPU-side overhead, reducing Trace Commit by ~100ms at APC 300 with negligible impact at APC 0 (only ~4K columns).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b26f810-a2da-49ad-94ae-b745d8ecf3f5","uuid":"50acd15c-0b98-4a45-a02d-51afed9f8d0e","timestamp":"2026-04-13T00:04:44.075Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"apc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n---\nplan.md\n---\n# 2026-04-13-1500-batch-stacking-scatter-kernel\n\nThe `stack_traces_into_expanded()` function in `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` iterates over every trace column (~106K at APC 300) issuing individual CUDA API calls (cudaMemcpyAsync or batch_expand_pad_wide kernel launch) per column. At ~1us CPU overhead per call, this loop costs ~100ms—about 25% of the 404ms Trace Commit phase and 6% of STARK excl trace. Replacing the per-column loop with a single batched scatter kernel that processes all column copies in one GPU launch eliminates this CPU-side overhead, reducing Trace Commit by ~100ms at APC 300 with negligible impact at APC 0 (only ~4K columns).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
