{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011EyVRRMArVgxhcGWr4kFyz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All steps complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n---\n\n**Generate & Plan Phase Complete**\n\n**Current performance (vs baseline):**\n| Config | Baseline | Current | Improvement |\n|--------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| APC 0 | 2153ms | 2148ms | 1.00x |\n| APC 100 | 2155ms | 1777ms | 1.21x |\n| APC 300 | 2455ms | 1731ms | 1.42x |\n\n**Selected optimization: Batch Stacking Scatter Kernel**\n\nThe `stack_traces_into_expanded()` function loops over ~106K trace columns at APC 300, issuing individual CUDA API calls per column. The CPU-side overhead (~1-5us per call) totals ~100-150ms — about 25% of Trace Commit time. A new CUDA scatter kernel processes all column copies in a single launch, reducing this to ~3ms.\n\n**Changes (5 files):**\n1. New CUDA kernel `stack_columns_kernel` in `matrix.cu`\n2. Rust FFI wrapper + `StackColDesc` struct in `cuda/matrix.rs`\n3. Restructured `stack_traces_into_expanded()` into 2-phase approach (build descriptors, then single kernel) in `stacked_pcs.rs`\n4. New error variants in `error.rs`\n5. Import cleanup in `stacked_pcs.rs`\n\n**Expected impact:** ~100-150ms savings at APC 300 (6-9% of STARK excl trace), negligible at APC 0.\n\n**Review status:** 2 rounds, no design-level blockers, prototype-ready."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":178592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":761},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b26f810-a2da-49ad-94ae-b745d8ecf3f5","uuid":"c311e798-3002-4dbe-b089-c7a72a7b2096"}
